course: dictionary
lesson: 3666
title: One spelling, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the same spelling can hide a different word. Fitch is a rare word with three meanings: a wild animal, a plant, and a paintbrush. The clues around it tell you which one is meant.
explain: Look at the words near it. Is the text about animals, farms, or painting? A nature lesson that mentions fur points to the animal. A room full of paint points to the brush. In «fitch fur», the word fur is a clue that a fitch is an animal.
explain: Watch out for names. In «stations on the Fitchburg Road», fitch is only part of a place name, Fitchburg, so it is not one of the three meanings. Capital letters and the words next to it are the clues. Then check: does your meaning make sense in the sentence?
fact: Fitch is a noun: a fitch, several fitches.
fact: «Fitch» can mean a polecat, a wild animal of the weasel family, or its fur.
fact: «Fitch» can also mean a kind of plant grown for seeds, a vetch or similar, which appears as «fitches» in old English Bibles.
fact: «Fitch» can mean a long-handled brush used by painters and signwriters.
fact: Fitch is a rare word, so when you meet it, read the clues before you decide.
exercise: In nature class, the teacher reads, «The fitch crept along the hedge, its brown fur glossy.» What is a fitch here? | *A polecat, a wild animal of the weasel family | A pebble on the beach | A bird that sings at dawn | A long brush for painting walls
exercise: «Mia dipped the fitch into the paint and drew a thin, neat line.» What is a fitch here? | A fish in the river | A polecat with brown fur | *A long-handled brush used by painters | A plant grown for seeds
exercise: Old Bibles mention «fitches» in a passage about sowing seeds. What does fitches mean here? | *A kind of plant grown for seeds, like a vetch | A wild animal | A beach of small pebbles | A paintbrush
test: «The painter cleaned the fitch before he put it away.» Which meaning fits? | A polecat | A pebble on the beach | *A long-handled brush | A plant grown for seeds
test: In «stations on the Fitchburg Road», what is fitch part of? | A polecat's den | A painter's tool | *A place name, Fitchburg | A kind of old plant
exam: Jayden finds fitch in a text about painting, nature and a town called Fitchburg. What should he do first? | Look up the meaning of every word in the book | *Read the clues around it, since the same spelling can mean a brush, an animal, a plant or part of a place name | Skip it, because context never helps with rare words | Guess the first meaning he sees and move on
